Check.Home.InactiveDetail=Check: whether the system is a Home edition. Home edition officially has no Remote Desktop host, though most systems can still create a twin session, so this is a notice only and never blocks startup.\nCurrent edition: {0}
Check.OldSystem.InactiveDetail=Check: whether wtsapi32.dll exports WTSEnableChildSessions (present since Windows 10 1803). This system has it, so nothing is reported.\nCurrent system: {0}
Check.TermDisabled.InactiveDetail=Check: whether the Remote Desktop service (TermService) start type is Disabled.\nCurrent start type: {0}
Check.TermStopped.InactiveDetail=Check: whether the Remote Desktop service (TermService) is running.\nCurrent state: {0}
Check.RdpOff.InactiveDetail=Check: whether fDenyTSConnections is 1 (group policy overrides the local setting). At 1 this PC does not listen for RDP and the twin cannot be created.\nCurrent value: {0}
Check.HelloOnly.InactiveDetail=Check: whether DevicePasswordLessBuildVersion is 2 (only Windows Hello sign-in). At 2 a Microsoft account has no usable password credential.\nCurrent value: {0}
Check.Wrapper.InactiveDetail=Check: whether the ServiceDll of TermService was replaced by a patch such as RDP Wrapper or SuperRDP. When it is, the stock Child Session and the patch exclude each other.\nCurrently points at: {0}
