Fix.ServiceKey.NeedRestart=The fields were written, but the service could not be restarted: {0}. Restart the Remote Desktop service manually and try again.
Fix.ServiceKey.Restored=ImagePath, ObjectName and the dependencies of TermService are back to the Windows defaults (dependencies were only appended; existing ones were kept).
Fix.Persistence.Nothing=There is nothing to clean up.
Fix.Persistence.Incomplete=Some task folders were denied, so the scan is incomplete and leftovers cannot be ruled out. Re-check as administrator and try again.
Fix.Persistence.PartialFailed=These entries could not be removed: {0}
Fix.Persistence.Removed=Removed {0} scheduled tasks and {1} autostart entries; backups are in: {2}
Fix.Persistence.RemovedIncomplete=Removed {0} scheduled tasks and {1} autostart entries; backups are in {2}. Some paths were denied, so the scan is incomplete and leftovers may remain.
Fix.RdpSecurity.AlreadyOk=No security setting is below its default; nothing to fix.
Fix.RdpSecurity.PartialFailed=These values could not be written: {0}
Fix.RdpSecurity.Restored=The lowered security settings are back at their defaults (higher values were left alone). Changes take effect when the Remote Desktop service next starts.
Fix.Termsrv.AlreadyOk=termsrv.dll matches the system component store; nothing to fix.
Fix.Termsrv.RestoredFromBackup=termsrv.dll was restored from {0} and the Remote Desktop service was restarted. The file that was in place before is saved at {1}.
Fix.Termsrv.RepairedBySfc=sfc has run ({0}); termsrv.dll now passes verification again.
Fix.Termsrv.SfcNotFixed=sfc has run ({0}), but the file still differs from the system component store. While termsrv.dll is in use by the service, sfc usually only replaces it after a reboot: restart the PC, then check again here. If it still fails, run DISM /Online /Cleanup-Image /RestoreHealth as administrator, then run sfc /scannow once more.
Fix.Termsrv.StopFailed=Could not stop the Remote Desktop service ({0}), so restoring from a backup was skipped. 
Fix.Termsrv.StopFailedNoRestart=; and the Remote Desktop service could not be restarted: {0}.
Fix.Termsrv.RestartCheck= The Remote Desktop service could not be restarted earlier; start it manually or reboot if you cannot connect.
Fix.Termsrv.RestartFailed=; but the Remote Desktop service could not be restored ({0}). Start "Remote Desktop Services" manually or reboot.
Fix.Termsrv.StateUnknown=could not query the Remote Desktop service state.
Fix.Termsrv.StillPending=the Remote Desktop service did not finish its state change within 30 seconds.
Fix.Termsrv.SfcMissing=sfc.exe was not found, so it cannot be repaired automatically.
Fix.Termsrv.SfcFailed=Could not start sfc. Run sfc /scannow manually as administrator.
Fix.Termsrv.SfcTimeout=sfc did not finish within 30 minutes and was given up on. Run sfc /scannow manually.
Fix.Termsrv.SfcClean=no integrity violations found
Fix.Termsrv.SfcRepaired=corrupted files were repaired
Fix.Termsrv.SfcCouldNotRepair=some files could not be repaired
Diag.FixHint.DllType=This writes ServiceDll back to the native termsrv.dll as REG_EXPAND_SZ and restarts the Remote Desktop service. The restart drops any current Remote Desktop connection, including a twin desktop you are using.
Diag.FixHint.ServiceKey=This restores ImagePath and ObjectName to the Windows defaults, appends the missing dependencies (RPCSS, StateRepository), then restarts the service. The restart drops any current Remote Desktop connection.
Diag.FixHint.Persistence=This exports the matched scheduled tasks as XML and the autostart entries as text into the backup folder, then deletes them. Once they are gone these tools can no longer switch the configuration back to the patched state at boot.
Diag.FixHint.RdpSecurity=This only raises values that are below the Windows default; anything already hardened to a higher value stays as it is. Changes take effect when the Remote Desktop service next starts; the service is not restarted.
Diag.FixHint.Termsrv=This first restores termsrv.dll from a backup the tool left behind (the copy is re-verified with sfc immediately and rolled back if it does not pass); if no usable backup exists it runs sfc /scannow. sfc usually takes 5-15 minutes and the panel keeps showing "Fixing…" meanwhile, so please do not close it. If the file is in use, the replacement may only happen after a reboot.
